    mscp:sourceId "125" ;
    mscp:sourceSection "m" ;
    mscp:title "CSV on the Web (CSVW)" .

msc:m126 a msct:m ;
    mscp:dataTypes msc:datatype4 ;
    mscp:description "An educational metadata profile for the description of teaching and learning resources, which is mainly based on schema.org or Learning Resource Metadata Initiative [LRMI] and also uses parts of Simple Knowledge Organization System [SKOS]. A JSON-LD-compliant data structure is defined in the form of a HTML specification, including a JSON schema against which data can be automatically checked for conformity with the profile." ;
    mscp:keywords <http://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/thesaurus/domain1> ;
    mscp:locations <https://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/msc/node/m/126/locations/1>,
        <https://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/msc/node/m/126/locations/2> ;
    mscp:namespaces <https://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/msc/node/m/126/namespaces/1> ;
    mscp:slug "amb-general-metadata-profile-for-educational-resources" ;
    mscp:sourceId "126" ;
    mscp:sourceSection "m" ;
    mscp:title "AMB (General metadata profile for educational resources)" .

msc:m128 a msct:m ;
    mscp:dataTypes msc:datatype2 ;
    mscp:description """Open Energy Metadata (OEMetadata) is a metadata standard for the energy domain.\r
It is an extensive set of metadata based on the tabular data package specifications and the FAIR principles. It is mainly developed for the Open Energy Platform (OEP).""" ;
    mscp:identifiers <https://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/msc/node/m/128/identifiers/1> ;
    mscp:keywords <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept194>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept9508>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept987> ;
    mscp:locations <https://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/msc/node/m/128/locations/1>,
        <https://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/msc/node/m/128/locations/2>,
        <https://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/msc/node/m/128/locations/3>,
        <https://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/msc/node/m/128/locations/4> ;
    mscp:slug "oemetadata-open-energy-metadata" ;
    mscp:sourceId "128" ;
    mscp:sourceSection "m" ;
    mscp:title "OEMetadata (Open Energy Metadata)" .

msc:m129 a msct:m ;
    mscp:dataTypes msc:datatype1,
        msc:datatype2 ;
    mscp:description "MOD (Metadata for Ontology Description and Publication Ontology) is a metadata schema designed to describe semantic artefacts, such as ontologies, vocabularies, and terminologies, in a standardized and FAIR-compliant way. Developed in the RDA Vocabulary Service Interest Group (VSIG) then within the FAIR-IMPACT EOSC project, MOD is based on DCAT2 and builds on existing metadata standards like DC, Schema.org, ADMS, etc. to provide a structured framework for capturing essential information about these artefacts, including their provenance, licensing, versioning, and usage. The schema facilitates interoperability between ontology repositories and enables better discovery, reuse, and integration of semantic resources in various domains. It is the baseline for MOD-API a Web service API specification for operations on semantic artefact catalogues. MOD is openly available on GitHub, where it is maintained and extended based on community input." ;
    mscp:keywords <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept10081>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept10614>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept12263>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept13408>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept13409>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept7984> ;
    mscp:locations <https://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/msc/node/m/129/locations/1>,
        <https://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/msc/node/m/129/locations/2>,
        <https://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/msc/node/m/129/locations/3> ;
    mscp:namespaces <https://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/msc/node/m/129/namespaces/1> ;
    mscp:slug "mod-metadata-for-ontology-description-and-publication-ontology" ;
    mscp:sourceId "129" ;
    mscp:sourceSection "m" ;
    mscp:title "MOD (Metadata for Ontology Description and Publication Ontology)" .

msc:m130 a msct:m ;
    mscp:description "CIMR was developed by the Metabolomics Standards Initiative (MSI) to specify guidelines for the minimum information to include when reporting metabolomics work. It was developed in textual form, but work is underway to develop a data model, exchange format and ontology for expressing the information in machine-actionable form." ;
    mscp:keywords <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept3954> ;
    mscp:locations <https://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/msc/node/m/130/locations/1> ;
    mscp:slug "cimr-core-information-for-metabolomics-reporting" ;
    mscp:sourceId "130" ;
    mscp:sourceSection "m" ;
    mscp:title "CIMR (Core Information for Metabolomics Reporting)" .

msc:m131 a msct:m ;
    mscp:description "GIATE is a minimum information checklist for transparently reporting the purpose, methods and results of the therapeutic experiments. Resources are provided for compiling metadata records in spreadsheet form (GIATE-TAB), rather than using a machine-readable serialization, though machine readability is one of the stated objectives for the checklist." ;
    mscp:keywords <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept219>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept241> ;
    mscp:slug "giate-guidelines-for-information-about-therapy-experiments" ;
    mscp:sourceId "131" ;
    mscp:sourceSection "m" ;
    mscp:title "GIATE (Guidelines for Information About Therapy Experiments)" ;
    mscp:versions <https://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/msc/node/m/131/versions/1> .

msc:m133 a msct:m ;
    mscp:dataTypes msc:datatype2 ;
    mscp:description """An internationally-adopted schema for describing geographic information and services. It provides information about the identification, the extent, the quality, the spatial and temporal schema, spatial reference, and distribution of digital geographic data.\r
\r
Sponsored by the International Standards Organisation, the first edition of ISO 19115 was published in 2023. \r
\r
An extension of ISO 19115 and the main changes are as follows:\r
\r
    — cross-references to other documents have been updated; in particular, ISO 19139:2007 has been updated to ISO/TS 19139-1:2019;\r
    — components have been reallocated to the relevant primary International Standards, notably ISO 19115-1:2014, ISO 19115-2:2019 and ISO 19103:2015;\r
    — additional packages and namespaces derived by the aggregation of packages defined in ISO 19115-1:2014 and ISO 19115-2:20091 have been removed;\r
    — tables have been consolidated in order to reduce repetition of information and to collocate information concerning requirements, conformance tests and the clauses to which they refer;\r
    — elements in the XML schemas for ISO 19115-1:2014 and ISO 19115-2:2019 have been reordered in order to align with the order of attributes in the associated data dictionaries. Appropriate XML stylesheets (XSLT) have been generated to assist in the transformation of XML records from records conforming to previous versions of the schemas. The conceptual models in the HMMG have been augmented to include the attribute ordering as set out in the data dictionaries in ISO 19115-1:2014 plus ISO 19115-1:2014/Amd 1:2018 and ISO 19115-1:2014/Amd 2:2020 and ISO 19115-2:2019.""" ;
    mscp:keywords <http://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/thesaurus/subdomain235>,
        <http://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/thesaurus/subdomain240>,
        <http://rdamsc.bath.ac.uk/thesaurus/subdomain250>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept11433>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept11459>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept11905>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept159>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept172>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept3269>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept6991>,
        <http://vocabularies.unesco.org/thesaurus/concept7430>,
